---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---

<Site
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Little Fight NYC builds for readable text, keyboard access, reduced motion and small screens. Contact us if something on this website gets in your way."
>
  <article class="policy shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>Accessibility</span>
    </nav>
    <p class="label">Updated October 9, 2026</p>
    <h1>
      MADE TO
      <br />
      BE USED.
    </h1>
    <p>
      This website is built toward WCAG 2.2 AA. That is a design and testing
      target, not a claim that automated testing can certify every person’s
      experience.
    </p>
    <h2>How the site works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Readable text with a 16-pixel minimum and responsive layouts.</li>
      <li>
        Keyboard navigation, visible focus and a skip link to the main content.
      </li>
      <li>
        Navigation and primary controls with targets of at least 44 pixels.
      </li>
      <li>
        Reduced-motion support and content that remains available without
        JavaScript.
      </li>
      <li>Form labels, field-specific errors and a clear draft state.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>If something gets in the way</h2>
    <p>
      Email{' '}
      <a href="mailto:hello@littlefightnyc.com?subject=Website%20accessibility">
        hello@littlefightnyc.com
      </a>{' '}
      or call <a href="tel:+16463600318">(646) 360-0318</a>. Include the page,
      what you were trying to do, and the browser or assistive technology if you
      know it. You can contact us directly without using the form.
    </p>
    <h2>External websites</h2>
    <p>
      The portfolio links lead to separate client sites. Their accessibility may
      differ from this website.
    </p>
  </article>
</Site>
